# Forbidden patterns for TS/JS/Vue files. Applied by .githooks/pre-commit.
# scaffold-extensions: ts tsx js jsx mjs cjs mts cts vue svelte
# Format: <regex><TAB><description>   (one per line; # comments ignored)
# Separator is TAB — patterns can contain literal `|` for ERE alternation.
# Patterns are case-SENSITIVE, scanned against the staged blob. Copy to your
# project as `.forbidden-patterns/frontend.txt`.

# --- Debug leaks ---
(^|[^A-Za-z_])console\.log[[:space:]]*\(	Use the project logger, not console.log
(^|[^A-Za-z_])debugger($|[^A-Za-z0-9_])	Remove debugger statement before committing
(^|[^A-Za-z_])alert[[:space:]]*\(	Don't ship alert() calls — use a proper UI dialog

# --- Test discipline ---
# A focused test silently skips the rest of the suite — CI goes green while
# almost nothing ran. The single most dangerous thing to commit in a test file.
(^|[^A-Za-z_.])(describe|it|test|context)\.only[[:space:]]*\(	Focused test (.only) silently skips the suite — remove before committing

# --- Type-checker escape hatches ---
@ts-ignore	Use @ts-expect-error with a justification, not @ts-ignore
@ts-nocheck	Do not disable type-checking for a whole file (@ts-nocheck)

# --- Linter escape hatches ---
# The lint twin of @ts-nocheck: one blanket `/* eslint-disable */` at the top of
# a file silences every rule eslint.config.js ships (no-floating-promises,
# no-explicit-any, the complexity caps, the import-hygiene rules) and both the
# hook and CI still exit 0 — the same "green because almost nothing ran" shape
# as a focused test. Only the FILE-WIDE, rule-less form is banned:
# `// eslint-disable-next-line <rule>` is the reviewable escape valve and stays
# legal, as does a named file-wide disable (`/* eslint-disable no-console */`).
/\*[[:space:]]*eslint-disable[[:space:]]*\*/	Blanket /* eslint-disable */ turns off every rule for the file — disable one named rule on one line instead

# --- Coverage escape hatches ---
# vitest.config.ts sets coverage provider `v8`, and --coverage-gate fails a PR on
# untested CHANGED lines. An ignore comment deletes the line from the gate's
# denominator instead of testing it, so the report reads 100% on code that never
# ran — cheaper than the assertion-free test, and invisible in the CI log (unlike
# a lowered threshold). Genuinely unexecutable code takes `scaffold-allow` and is
# named in the handoff summary like any other suppression.
(/\*|//)[[:space:]]*(istanbul|[cv]8)[[:space:]]+ignore	Coverage ignore comment removes the line from the patch-coverage gate — write the test, or scaffold-allow a genuinely unexecutable branch

# --- Unfinished stubs ---
# The TS twin of rust.txt's todo!()/unimplemented!() rules. A `throw` inhabits any
# return type and satisfies noImplicitReturns, so a stub type-checks, lints, and
# is fully covered by a test that asserts only the throw — every mechanical signal
# reads as complete while nothing is implemented.
throw[[:space:]]+new[[:space:]]+Error\([[:space:]]*["'`]([Uu]n|[Nn]ot[[:space:]_-]*)[Ii]mplemented	Unfinished stub left in — implement it or open a ticket

# --- Security ---
dangerouslySetInnerHTML	dangerouslySetInnerHTML is an XSS vector — sanitize or render as text
(^|[^A-Za-z-])v-html[[:space:]]*=	Vue v-html is an XSS vector — sanitize or render with {{ }}/text
\{@html[[:space:]]	Svelte {@html} is an XSS vector — sanitize (DOMPurify) or render as text
https?://(localhost|127\.0\.0\.1)	No hardcoded localhost/127.0.0.1 URLs — read from config/env
NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED	Never disable TLS certificate validation — fix the cert/CA instead (MITM risk)
rejectUnauthorized[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*false	rejectUnauthorized: false disables TLS validation — add the CA to the trust store instead
\.(inner|outer)HTML[[:space:]]*\+?=([^=]|$)	Raw innerHTML/outerHTML assignment is an XSS sink — sanitize (DOMPurify) or set textContent

# Optional: forbid TODO/FIXME/XXX in one line via regex alternation.
# (^|[^A-Za-z_])(TODO|FIXME|XXX)($|[^A-Za-z0-9_])	TODO/FIXME/XXX not allowed — open a ticket instead

# Optional: forbid dynamic code execution (eval / new Function).
# (^|[^A-Za-z_.])(eval|Function)[[:space:]]*\(	Avoid eval()/new Function() — arbitrary-code-execution risk

# Optional (opt-in): never commit an enabled auth-bypass flag. Generic
# alternation — adjust the flag names to your project.
# (BYPASS_AUTH|DISABLE_AUTH|SKIP_AUTH|AUTH_DISABLED)[[:space:]]*[:=][[:space:]]*(true|1)	Auth-bypass flag enabled — never commit a true value
